  "result": "Perfect! All 93 tests pass. I've successfully implemented line discounts for the invoicing system:\n\n**Updated files:**\n\n1. **`src/errors.js`** - Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code\n\n2. **`src/invoices.js`** - Updated three functions:\n   - `createInvoice()` - Now accepts `discountPercent` (0-100, including decimals) on line input; defaults to 0\n   - `addLine()` - Now accepts `discountPercent` with validation; defaults to 0 for new lines\n   - `invoiceTotals()` - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n     - discount = sum of (line total \u00d7 discountPercent / 100) for each line\n     - total = subtotal - discount\n     - All amounts clamped at 0 using `Math.max(0, value)`\n     - Fractional cents rounded with `roundCents()`\n\n**Test coverage (14 new discount tests):**\n- createInvoice accepts/validates discountPercent\n- addLine accepts/validates discountPercent\n- invoiceTotals calculates multiple line discounts correctly\n- Decimal discounts (12.5%) handled with rounding\n- 100% discount scenario (total becomes 0)\n- Clamping at 0 for defensive programming\n- Render test with discounted invoices\n\n**Key design decisions implemented:**\n- Discount validation: must be a number from 0 to 100 (rejects negative or >100)\n- Line discounts are calculated independently per line using banker's rounding\n- All computed amounts are clamped at 0 (never negative)\n- discountPercent defaults to 0 when not provided\n\nAll 93 tests pass (79 previous + 14 new discount tests).",
